<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: German, U.S. firm to create 100 jobs in Leitrim.</title>
<headline>German, U.S. firm to create 100 jobs in Leitrim.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 4.25 million Irish pound investment by two overseas companies will create 100 jobs in County Leitrim, Irish enterprise and employment minister Richard Bruton said on Monday.</p>
<p>German-based Westmark, a manufacturer of mechanical kitchen aids, will invest three million Irish pounds and create 88 new jobs over the next four years, Bruton said in a statement.</p>
<p>U.S.-based Lilly Industries will create an additional 12 jobs from a 1.25 million punt investment to establish an industrial coatings facility.</p>
<p>The jobs are being created with the support of industrial development agency, IDA Ireland.</p>
<p>--Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
